.TH OPENHAMSHACK-RADIO 1 "2026-10-04" "openhamshack-radio" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openhamshack-radio \- all-band amateur radio SDR transceiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openhamshack-radio
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
OpenHamShack Radio is a native PyQt6 desktop transceiver for the amateur bands,
160 m to 6 cm: SSB, CW, AM, FM with CTCSS, repeater shifts and the 1750 Hz
toneburst, FT8, FT4, PSK31/63/125, RTTY, FreeDV and SSTV. A radio engine
owns the SDR and does all the signal processing; a Qt window is the whole
user interface; both run in one process.
.PP
It holds every transmission inside the UK licence class set in Settings
(Foundation, Intermediate or Full), at no more than that class's power
there as estimated from the power chain entered per band, refuses the
beacon and satellite sub-bands, and warns when a transmission leaves what
the RSGB band plan intends.
.PP
It drives the ADALM-Pluto family (Pluto, Pluto+, LibreSDR, Pluto nano) on
VHF and up and the Hermes-Lite 2 on HF; any SoapySDR receiver for receive
only. With no hardware attached it runs against simulated bands.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run the engine without opening a window: print one status line a second
to standard output instead. Nothing in this mode ever keys the
transmitter.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " DEVICE"
Override the configured device for this run only. One of
.BR sim ", " pluto ", " hl2 " or " soapy .
.TP
.BI \-\-band " BAND"
Start on this band (160m ... 10m, 4m, 2m, 70cm, 23cm, 13cm, 9cm, 6cm).
.TP
.BI \-\-rf " MHZ"
Start on this frequency.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " MODE"
Start in this mode (usb, lsb, cw, am, fm, ft8 ...).
.TP
.BI \-\-seconds " N"
Stop after
.I N
seconds (0, the default: run until interrupted).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audio
Run with the null audio backend: no sound card is opened.
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log at INFO level instead of the default WARNING.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the built-in usage summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/openhamshack-radio/config.json
Persisted settings. Overridden by the
.B OHS_RADIO_CONF
environment variable.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/openhamshack-radio/
The log and received SSTV images. Overridden by the
.B OHS_RADIO_DATA
environment variable.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OHS_RADIO_CONF
Path to the config file, in place of the default under
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B OHS_RADIO_DATA
Path to the data directory, in place of the default under
.IR ~/.local/share .
.TP
.BR OHSRADIO_CONF ", " OHSRADIO_DATA
The names these had before the OpenHamShack rename; still read when
the OHS_RADIO_ ones are not set.
.PP
An installation from before the rename kept its files under
.IR ~/.config/openhamshack-ham " and " ~/.local/share/openhamshack-ham .
The first start of this version moves both to the new names and leaves
a link at each old one; nothing is copied and nothing deleted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on a clean stop;
.B 1
if the engine could not start;
.B 2
if no window is available (the message says to pass \-\-headless).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openhamshack-nb (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Brian Henderson
